From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve pkg-config variables during CMake configuration

configure_file expands both @VAR@ and ${VAR} by default. The latter form
is also pkg-config syntax: consuming ${libdir} and ${includedir} produces
empty -L and -I/libdxfrw flags even though the headers were installed.
Use @ONLY and @CMAKE_*@ substitutions so pkg-config resolves its own
variables at consumption time, including a staged install sysroot.
Downstream packaging correction; no build target or test is removed.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -96 +96 @@
-configure_file(${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/libdxfrw.pc.in libdxfrw.pc)
+configure_file(${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/libdxfrw.pc.in libdxfrw.pc @ONLY)
--- a/libdxfrw.pc.in
+++ b/libdxfrw.pc.in
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-prefix=${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}
-exec_prefix=${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}
-libdir=${CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_LIBDIR}
-includedir=${CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_INCLUDEDIR}
+prefix=@CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX@
+exec_prefix=@CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX@
+libdir=@CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_LIBDIR@
+includedir=@CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_INCLUDEDIR@
@@ -8 +8 @@
-Version: ${PROJECT_VERSION}
+Version: @PROJECT_VERSION@
